#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0054 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "A BDS dataset legitimately holds many records per subject, which is exactly why this rule is ADSL-only: Data_Structures.Include: [SUBJECT LEVEL ANALYSIS DATASET]. RULING-NEUTRAL: the sheet cell is the single token 'ADSL', so BDS is outside it on any reading. Rows deliberately carry DUPLICATE USUBJIDs (the firing shape), so the skip is attributable to scope alone."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB  | 4.1
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | GLUC | 5.5
